<div id="non-linear-regression-with-decision-trees" class="section level1">
<h1>Non-Linear Regression with Decision Trees</h1>
<p>The regression tree is pruned using cross-validation and is limited
to at most five splits for a clear, interpretable visualization.</p>
<div class="sourceCode" id="cb66"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb66-1"><a href="#cb66-1" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">set.seed</span>(<span class="dv">2026</span>)</span>
<span id="cb66-2"><a href="#cb66-2" tabindex="-1"></a></span>
<span id="cb66-3"><a href="#cb66-3" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="co"># Grow a candidate tree first.</span></span>
<span id="cb66-4"><a href="#cb66-4" tabindex="-1"></a>fit_tree_full <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> rpart<span class="sc">::</span><span class="fu">rpart</span>(</span>
<span id="cb66-5"><a href="#cb66-5" tabindex="-1"></a>  HeatingLoad <span class="sc">~</span> .,</span>
<span id="cb66-6"><a href="#cb66-6" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="at">data =</span> train_data,</span>
<span id="cb66-7"><a href="#cb66-7" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="at">method =</span> <span class="st">&quot;anova&quot;</span>,</span>
<span id="cb66-8"><a href="#cb66-8" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="at">control =</span> rpart<span class="sc">::</span><span class="fu">rpart.control</span>(</span>
<span id="cb66-9"><a href="#cb66-9" tabindex="-1"></a>    <span class="at">cp =</span> <span class="fl">0.001</span>,</span>
<span id="cb66-10"><a href="#cb66-10" tabindex="-1"></a>    <span class="at">minsplit =</span> <span class="dv">60</span>,</span>
<span id="cb66-11"><a href="#cb66-11" tabindex="-1"></a>    <span class="at">minbucket =</span> <span class="dv">25</span>,</span>
<span id="cb66-12"><a href="#cb66-12" tabindex="-1"></a>    <span class="at">maxdepth =</span> <span class="dv">6</span>,</span>
<span id="cb66-13"><a href="#cb66-13" tabindex="-1"></a>    <span class="at">xval =</span> <span class="dv">10</span></span>
<span id="cb66-14"><a href="#cb66-14" tabindex="-1"></a>  )</span>
<span id="cb66-15"><a href="#cb66-15" tabindex="-1"></a>)</span>
<span id="cb66-16"><a href="#cb66-16" tabindex="-1"></a></span>
<span id="cb66-17"><a href="#cb66-17" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="co"># Review the cross-validated error for candidate tree sizes.</span></span>
<span id="cb66-18"><a href="#cb66-18" tabindex="-1"></a>rpart<span class="sc">::</span><span class="fu">printcp</span>(fit_tree_full)</span></code></pre></div>
<pre><code>## 
## Regression tree:
## rpart::rpart(formula = HeatingLoad ~ ., data = train_data, method = &quot;anova&quot;, 
##     control = rpart::rpart.control(cp = 0.001, minsplit = 60, 
##         minbucket = 25, maxdepth = 6, xval = 10))
## 
## Variables actually used in tree construction:
## [1] GlazingArea             GlazingAreaDistribution OverallHeight          
## [4] RelativeCompactness     SurfaceArea             WallArea               
## 
## Root node error: 64818/614 = 105.57
## 
## n= 614 
## 
##           CP nsplit rel error   xerror      xstd
## 1  0.8009831      0  1.000000 1.002822 0.0349985
## 2  0.0860949      1  0.199017 0.200243 0.0132687
## 3  0.0256596      2  0.112922 0.114587 0.0079947
## 4  0.0138982      3  0.087262 0.089078 0.0057265
## 5  0.0122374      4  0.073364 0.077912 0.0054274
## 6  0.0066330      5  0.061127 0.062594 0.0041249
## 7  0.0060255      6  0.054494 0.059243 0.0038763
## 8  0.0042907      7  0.048468 0.051184 0.0037570
## 9  0.0032384      8  0.044178 0.048138 0.0036707
## 10 0.0029376      9  0.040939 0.045986 0.0035924
## 11 0.0027833     10  0.038002 0.044473 0.0035574
## 12 0.0019243     11  0.035218 0.042148 0.0034927
## 13 0.0014894     12  0.033294 0.040526 0.0035231
## 14 0.0013543     13  0.031805 0.040579 0.0035222
## 15 0.0010000     14  0.030450 0.039520 0.0033472</code></pre>
<div class="sourceCode" id="cb68"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb68-1"><a href="#cb68-1" tabindex="-1"></a>old_par <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu">par</span>(</span>
<span id="cb68-2"><a href="#cb68-2" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="at">col =</span> plot_palette[<span class="dv">1</span>],</span>
<span id="cb68-3"><a href="#cb68-3" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="at">col.axis =</span> plot_palette[<span class="dv">1</span>],</span>
<span id="cb68-4"><a href="#cb68-4" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="at">col.lab =</span> plot_palette[<span class="dv">1</span>]</span>
<span id="cb68-5"><a href="#cb68-5" tabindex="-1"></a>)</span>
<span id="cb68-6"><a href="#cb68-6" tabindex="-1"></a>rpart<span class="sc">::</span><span class="fu">plotcp</span>(fit_tree_full, <span class="at">main =</span> <span class="st">&quot;&quot;</span>)</span></code></pre></div>
<div class="figure" style="text-align: center">
<img role="img" aria-label="Cross-validated error used to guide regression-tree pruning" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Cross-validated error used to guide regression-tree pruning" width="1200" />
<p class="caption">
Cross-validated error used to guide regression-tree pruning
</p>
</div>
<div class="sourceCode" id="cb69"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb69-1"><a href="#cb69-1" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">par</span>(old_par)</span>
<span id="cb69-2"><a href="#cb69-2" tabindex="-1"></a></span>
<span id="cb69-3"><a href="#cb69-3" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="co"># Keep the final explanatory tree compact. Among candidate trees with at most</span></span>
<span id="cb69-4"><a href="#cb69-4" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="co"># five splits, choose the one with the smallest cross-validated error.</span></span>
<span id="cb69-5"><a href="#cb69-5" tabindex="-1"></a>cp_table <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> fit_tree_full<span class="sc">$</span>cptable</span>
<span id="cb69-6"><a href="#cb69-6" tabindex="-1"></a>max_display_splits <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="dv">5</span></span>
<span id="cb69-7"><a href="#cb69-7" tabindex="-1"></a></span>
<span id="cb69-8"><a href="#cb69-8" tabindex="-1"></a>eligible_rows <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu">which</span>(cp_table[, <span class="st">&quot;nsplit&quot;</span>] <span class="sc">&lt;=</span> max_display_splits)</span>
<span id="cb69-9"><a href="#cb69-9" tabindex="-1"></a></span>
<span id="cb69-10"><a href="#cb69-10" tabindex="-1"></a>selected_row <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> eligible_rows[</span>
<span id="cb69-11"><a href="#cb69-11" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="fu">which.min</span>(cp_table[eligible_rows, <span class="st">&quot;xerror&quot;</span>])</span>
<span id="cb69-12"><a href="#cb69-12" tabindex="-1"></a>]</span>
<span id="cb69-13"><a href="#cb69-13" tabindex="-1"></a></span>
<span id="cb69-14"><a href="#cb69-14" tabindex="-1"></a>selected_cp <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> cp_table[selected_row, <span class="st">&quot;CP&quot;</span>]</span>
<span id="cb69-15"><a href="#cb69-15" tabindex="-1"></a>fit_tree <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> rpart<span class="sc">::</span><span class="fu">prune</span>(fit_tree_full, <span class="at">cp =</span> selected_cp)</span>
<span id="cb69-16"><a href="#cb69-16" tabindex="-1"></a></span>
<span id="cb69-17"><a href="#cb69-17" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">cat</span>(<span class="st">&quot;Selected pruning CP:&quot;</span>, selected_cp, <span class="st">&quot;</span><span class="sc">\n</span><span class="st">&quot;</span>)</span></code></pre></div>
<pre><code>## Selected pruning CP: 0.006633035</code></pre>
<div class="sourceCode" id="cb71"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb71-1"><a href="#cb71-1" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">cat</span>(<span class="st">&quot;Selected number of splits:&quot;</span>, cp_table[selected_row, <span class="st">&quot;nsplit&quot;</span>], <span class="st">&quot;</span><span class="sc">\n</span><span class="st">&quot;</span>)</span></code></pre></div>
<pre><code>## Selected number of splits: 5</code></pre>
<div class="sourceCode" id="cb73"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb73-1"><a href="#cb73-1" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">cat</span>(</span>
<span id="cb73-2"><a href="#cb73-2" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="st">&quot;Terminal nodes before pruning:&quot;</span>,</span>
<span id="cb73-3"><a href="#cb73-3" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="fu">sum</span>(fit_tree_full<span class="sc">$</span>frame<span class="sc">$</span>var <span class="sc">==</span> <span class="st">&quot;&lt;leaf&gt;&quot;</span>),</span>
<span id="cb73-4"><a href="#cb73-4" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="st">&quot;</span><span class="sc">\n</span><span class="st">&quot;</span></span>
